Subject: [PATCH] rtw89: build fw.c at -O2

With -O3 the compiler inlines rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_enqueue into
rtw89_fw_cmd_ofld_udelay, constant-propagates a value into FIELD_PREP and
trips the compile-time overflow check (__field_overflow) in bitfield.h.
The same file builds cleanly at -O2. Lower the optimisation level for this
one object only; the rest of the kernel stays at -O3.

Found building 7.2 for SkillFishOS on 2026-08-18.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/Makefile
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw89/Makefile
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+# fw.c does not build at -O3: inlining trips the FIELD_PREP overflow check.
+CFLAGS_fw.o += -O2
+
